# Intent: The Apps wall and the Games wall look inviting. Each tile fills the zone (two columns of 154 by 90 px with 4 px gaps, the page dots in the strip under them) and has its own accent color, a large picture drawn from LVGL shapes when the wall opens (Color Memory's four colored quarters, a mole popping out of a mound, a tic-tac-toe grid with an X and an O, a pulse ring with an arrow for Do It, a fist, an open hand and scissors, a dark 8 ball with a triangle, two dice and a coin; Timers, Alarms, Clock, Quick actions, Pictures, Dashboard, Dance and Lock each have theirs) and the title in the 24 px font on a dark plate (a long title wraps on a taller plate in the 16 px font). The best score is a small pill in the corner of a game tile. A press brightens the tile and the tiles open one frame brighter, then settle. New host call game_id(i) names the game for its picture; an unknown game gets a play triangle. No bitmap and no font are added: the shapes are created when the wall opens and freed with it.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_apps_core.h, maipai_apps.cc, maipai_pages.h, maipai_pages_unit.cc (ours)
# Check after a flash: Apps (sheet, Apps tile) and Games show colored tiles with pictures and 24 px titles, the dots under the tiles, nothing else behind the wall.
# Kconfig: none

